    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the string membership tier with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Removed the `membershipTier` string field (BRONZE/SILVER/GOLD enum) from the owner response schema and replaced it with `membershipLevel` (integer, `int32`, minimum 1, maximum 3), documenting the new derivation rule. Since the DTOs are generated from this spec by the openapi-generator, this drives the `OwnerDto` API change and drops the old `MembershipTierEnum`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Retargeted the mapping from `membershipTier` to `membershipLevel` and rewrote the derivation method:\n   - start at 1\n   - `+1` when an email is present (non-blank)\n   - `+1` when `namesakeCount` is 0\n   - capped at 3 (`Math.min(level, 3)`), leaving level 4 reserved for tenure\n\n   The old household-based GOLD/SILVER/BRONZE logic and its now-unused `householdMemberCount` helper and `ownerRepository` dependency were removed (along with the now-dead imports).\n\nOn the audit line: the create audit line (`AuditOwnerCreated`) records id, customerCode and registrationDate \u2014 it never recorded the tier, so there was nothing to convert to the level there. Nothing else in the codebase referenced the tier.\n\n**Test result:** `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `AcceptanceTest.coreNumericLevel` asserts `membershipLevel == 3` for an owner with an email and a unique name, and it passes. `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
